More minor things:

-) Some rogue versions use the same command for putting on armor and
	putting on rings and other magic things, and likewise use 
	one command for taking them off.  Simplifies things a bit.

-) Various people have complained that you can't tell one dog from
	another.  Perhaps when you tame a dog or other monster it
	should be highlighted?

-) When you're searching or waiting or whatever, you should have
	the ability to stop when a monster comes in the room or near
	you, rather than when it succeeds in hitting you.  Maybe
	make it an option.  Certainly these things should stop any
	time you get a message about becoming hungry, weak, etc.

-) There are a lot of new rules that have happened in version 3.0.
	Since not everyone reads the source code (either through
	laziness or lack of access), it would be nice if there were
	some way to tell the user.  At minimum, interesting rules
	should go in the rumors file or the Oracle.  For example,
	knights lose luck points when they do unchivalrous things,
	and the new rules about Praying belong there.

	Things that change luck are very important, and for many of
	them the only way you find out is reading the source.
	Perhaps most of them should give the user a message, whether
	obvious ("You feel lucky!" - hallucinated = "Feeling Lucky
	Today, Punk?") or more subtle, like the messages you get
	when the Gods like your Offerings.  "That wasn't very Nice!"

-) It would be nice if the version numbering scheme changed a bit,
	so that the new patch becomes 3.6 instead of 3.0.6.

